### 📥 Isko Upload Kaise Kare?

1. Apne VS Code ya Notepad mein ek naya file banao jiska naam **`README.md`** rakho.
2. Upar wala pura code copy karke isme paste karo aur **Save** karo.
3. Ab apne terminal mein ye commands run karo:

```bash
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: add detailed project README"
git push origin main
Tumhare GitHub repo par ek bahut hi shandar aur professional README dikhne lagega! Interviewer isko dekh kar hi impress ho jayega.

Ab bolo, kya main Database Schema (Phase 1) ka code de doon?

gigitnore dfile deateld
Bhai, ye raha tumhare project ke liye ek ekdum professional aur detailed .gitignore file ka code.

Kyunki tumhare paas Python (Backend), React (Frontend), Database (SQLite) aur Gemini API (.env) sab kuch hai, toh is file mein maine saari chizein add kar di hain taaki tumhari API keys, heavy folders (node_modules), aur local database kabhi bhi galti se GitHub par upload na ho jayein.

Isko copy karke apne project ke root folder (main folder jahan README.md hai) mein .gitignore naam se save kar do.

📄 Code for .gitignore
gitignore
# ==========================================
# 1. PYTHON / BACKEND (FastAPI)
# ==========================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Virtual Environments
venv/
env/
.venv/
ENV/

# Environment Variables (API Keys, Secrets)
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.production

# Python Testing & Coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Jupyter Notebooks (if used)
.ipynb_checkpoints

# ==========================================
# 2. DATABASES & LOCAL DATA
# ==========================================
# SQLite Databases
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
database/sqlite/*.db

# ChromaDB Vector Store local data
chroma_db/
chroma/
backend/data/chroma/

# Uploaded Documents (Prevent pushing heavy PDFs)
backend/data/uploads/*
backend/data/processed/*
!backend/data/uploads/.gitkeep
!backend/data/processed/.gitkeep

# ==========================================
# 3. REACT / FRONTEND (Node.js)
# ==========================================
# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Production build
frontend/build/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Environment variables (Frontend)
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.development.local
frontend/.env.test.local
frontend/.env.production.local

# ==========================================
# 4. IDE & CODE EDITORS
# ==========================================
# VS Code
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/

# PyCharm / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Mac OS X
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ==========================================
# 5. LOGS & TEMP FILES
# ==========================================
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ==========================================
# 6. MISC (Docker, Coverage, etc.)
# ==========================================
# Docker (if used locally)
.dockerignore
docker-compose.override.yml

# Cache
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.eslintcache
